# Code Style

## Imports

- `always_use_package_imports` — no relative imports across packages
- `prefer_single_quotes` for strings
- Import order: `dart:` → `package:flutter/` → external `package:` → internal `package:` → relative

## Naming

| Item | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Files | `snake_case.dart` | `auth_bloc.dart` |
| Classes | `PascalCase` | `AuthBloc` |
| Constants | `camelCase` | `loginPath` |
| Routes class | `abstract final class` | `AuthRoutes` |
| Utility classes | `abstract final class` + private ctor | `TypeScale._()` |

## Structure

- One barrel file per package root: `lib/<package>.dart`
- Max 300 lines per file — split into `part` files if longer
- No commented-out code in committed files
- Avoid `dynamic` — use generics or sealed types

## BLoC File Layout

Consistent per package — either:
- `part` files: `auth_bloc.dart` + `part 'auth_event.dart'` + `part 'auth_state.dart'`
- Separate files: `auth_bloc.dart`, `auth_event.dart`, `auth_state.dart`
